(and selling, and no longer as before a science of Things howsoever) Tj T*
(manipulated for and in their market.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For another thing, before beginning to write out the first word of) Tj T*
(that book, I believed myself to have made sure, by repeated and) Tj T*
(multiform inductions, of this deepest truth in the whole Science,) Tj T*
(which was a little after embodied \(I hope I may even say _embalmed_\)) Tj T*
(in a phrase taking its proper place in the book itself,--_A market for) Tj T*
(Products is products in Market_. The fundamental thus tersely) Tj T*
(expressed may be formulated more at length in this way: One cannot) Tj T*
(Sell without at the same instant and in the same act Buying, nor Buy) Tj T*
(anything without simultaneously Selling something else; because in) Tj T*
(Buying one pays for what he buys, which is Selling, and in Selling one) Tj T*
(must take pay for what is sold, which is Buying. As these universal) Tj T*
(actions among men are always voluntary, there must be also an) Tj T*
(universal motive leading up to them; this motive on the part of both) Tj T*
(parties to each and every Sale can be no other than the mutual) Tj T*
(satisfaction derivable to both; the inference, accordingly, is easy) Tj T*
(and invincible, that governmental restrictions on Sales, or) Tj T*
(prohibitions of them, must lessen the satisfactions and retard the) Tj T*
(progress of mankind.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Organizing strictly all the matter of my book along these two lines of) Tj T*
(Personality and Reciprocity, notwithstanding much in it that was) Tj T*
(crude and more that was redundant and something that was ill-reasoned) Tj T*
(and unsound, the book made on account of this original mode of) Tj T*
(treatment an immediate impression upon the public, particularly upon) Tj T*
(teachers and pupils; new streaks of light could not but be cast from) Tj T*
(these new points of view, upon such topics especially as Land and) Tj T*
(Money and Foreign Trade; and nothing is likely ever to rob the author) Tj T*
(of the satisfaction, which he is willing to share with the public, of) Tj T*
(having contributed something of importance both in substance and in) Tj T*
(feature to the permanent up-building of that Science, which comes) Tj T*
(closer, it may be, to the homes and happiness and progress of the) Tj T*
(People, than any other science. And let it be said in passing, that) Tj T*
(there is one consideration well-fitted to stimulate and to reward each) Tj T*
(patient and competent scientific inquirer, no matter what that science) Tj T*
(may be in which he labors, namely, this: Any just generalization, made) Tj T*
(and fortified inductively, is put thereby beyond hazard of essential) Tj T*
(change for all time; for this best of reasons, that God has) Tj T*
(constructed the World and Men on everlasting lines of Order.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(As successive editions of this first book were called for, and as its) Tj T*
(many defects were brought out into the light through teaching my own) Tj T*
(classes from it year after year, occasion was taken to revise it and) Tj T*
(amend it and in large parts to rewrite it again and again; until, in) Tj T*
(1883, and for the eighteenth edition, it was recast from bottom up for) Tj T*
(wholly new plates, and a riper title was ventured upon,--"Political) Tj T*
(Economy,"--instead of the original more tentative "Elements." Since) Tj T*
(then have been weeded out the slight typographical and other minute) Tj T*
(errors, and the book stands now in its ultimate shape.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
