(My excellent publishers, who have always been keenly and wisely alive) Tj T*
(to my interests as an author, suggested several times after the) Tj T*
(success of the first book was reasonably assured, that a second and) Tj T*
(smaller one should be written out, with an especial eye to the needs) Tj T*
(of high schools and academies and colleges for a text-book within) Tj T*
(moderate limits, yet soundly based and covering in full outline the) Tj T*
(whole subject. This is the origin of the "Introduction to Political) Tj T*
(Economy," first published in 1877, twelve years after the other. Its) Tj T*
(success as a text-book and as a book of reading for young people has) Tj T*
(already justified, and will doubtless continue to justify in the) Tj T*
(future, the forethought of its promoters. It has found a place in many) Tj T*
(popular libraries, and in courses of prescribed reading. Twice it has) Tj T*
(been carefully corrected and somewhat enlarged, and is now in its) Tj T*
(final form. In the preface to the later editions of the "Introduction") Tj T*
(may be found the following sentence, which expresses a feeling not) Tj T*
(likely to undergo any change in the time to come:--"I have long been,) Tj T*
(and am still, ambitious that these books of mine may become the) Tj T*
(horn-books of my countrymen in the study of this fascinating Science.") Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Why, then, should I have undertaken of my own motion a new and third) Tj T*
(book on Political Economy, and attempted to mark the completion of the) Tj T*
(third cycle of a dozen years each of teaching it, by offering to the) Tj T*
(public the present volume? One reason is implied in the title,) Tj T*
("_Principles of Political Economy_." There are three extended) Tj T*
(historical chapters in the earlier book, occupying more than) Tj T*
(one-quarter of its entire space, which were indeed novel, which cost) Tj T*
(me wide research and very great labor, and which have also proven) Tj T*
(useful and largely illustrative of almost every phase of Economics;) Tj T*
(but I wanted to leave behind me one book of about the same size as) Tj T*
(that, devoted exclusively to the Principles of the Science, and using) Tj T*
(History only incidentally to illustrate in passing each topic as it) Tj T*
(came under review. For a college text-book as this is designed to) Tj T*
(become, and for a book of reading and reference for technical) Tj T*
(purposes, it seems better that all the space should be taken up by) Tj T*
(purely scientific discussion and illustration. This does not mean,) Tj T*
(however, that great pains have not been taken in every part to make) Tj T*
(this book also easily intelligible, and as readable and interesting as) Tj T*
(such careful discussions can be made.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A second reason is, to provide for myself a fresh text-book to teach) Tj T*
(from. My mind has become quite too thoroughly familiarized with the) Tj T*
(other, even down to the very words, by so long a course of instructing) Tj T*
(from it, for the best results in the class-room. Accordingly, a new) Tj T*
(plan of construction has been adopted. Instead of the fourteen) Tj T*
(chapters there, there are but seven chapters here. Not a page nor a) Tj T*
(paragraph as such has been copied from either of the preceding books.) Tj T*
(Single sentences, and sometimes several of them together, when they) Tj T*
(exactly fitted the purposes of the new context, have been incorporated) Tj T*
(here and there, in what is throughout both in form and style a new) Tj T*
(book, neither an enlargement nor an abridgment nor a recasting of any) Tj T*
(other. I anticipate great pleasure in the years immediately to come) Tj T*
(from the handling with my classes, who have always been of much) Tj T*
ET
