(famous "Mind-cure." The mind is indeed higher than the body, but) Tj T*
(bodily maladies must be treated as such, or the patient will die; the) Tj T*
(imperatives of Ethics are certainly superior to the profitables of) Tj T*
(Economics, but the latter are well able to take care of themselves on) Tj T*
(their own ground; Religion is loftier than Morals, but it becomes a) Tj T*
(very poor substitute for morals in the daily routine of life.) Tj T*
(_Similia similibus curantur._ Economical evils can only be removed by) Tj T*
