(CHAPTER IV.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(COMMERCIAL CREDITS.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Political Economy is the Science of Sales; and because it _is_ the) Tj T*
(science of sales, its definitions and principles must cover equally) Tj T*
(all cases of sales actually occurring or possible to occur. We have) Tj T*
(seen repeatedly, that only three kinds of things are ever bought and) Tj T*
(sold, or ever will be, and these are Commodities and Services and) Tj T*
(Claims. The first two kinds have been fully elucidated already in the) Tj T*
(two preceding chapters, and it belongs to the present chapter to) Tj T*
(explain and illustrate clearly the peculiarities of the third kind of) Tj T*
(things salable. Ours is the only science that has to do with the) Tj T*
(motives and facts and economic results of all sales as such.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The discussions of the present chapter will proceed orderly through) Tj T*
(the following topics:--) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(    _The Nature of Credit._) Tj T*
(    _The Forms of Credit._) Tj T*
(    _The Advantages of Credit._) Tj T*
(    _The Disadvantages of Credit._) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. Certain things are essential in every sale of anything, and of) Tj T*
(course are common to all sales of everything, such as two persons and) Tj T*
(two desires and two estimates and two renderings; while there are) Tj T*
(certain _peculiarities_ in the sale of things belonging to each of the) Tj T*
(three special classes of things salable; for example, in the sale of a) Tj T*
(commodity there is a rendering of a tangible object that has been) Tj T*
(prepared for sale in past time, and in the sale of a service a) Tj T*
(rendering of an intangible something wholly in the present time; while) Tj T*
(in the sale of a credit there are likewise two peculiarities, one of) Tj T*
(them relating to future time and the other to a special trust felt in) Tj T*
(a person by some other person. We must now study these two) Tj T*
(peculiarities with care; and, mastering these, we shall be master of) Tj T*
(the Nature of Credit.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(a. Some sales are consummated at once, the things exchanged and the) Tj T*
(ownership in them are mutually passed over then and there, the) Tj T*
(reciprocal satisfactions are entered upon immediately, and there is at) Tj T*
(once an economical end.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(For example, one neighbor sells another a peck of green peas and takes) Tj T*
(in pay a peck of new potatoes, both vegetables may be cooked for) Tj T*
(dinner in the respective families the same day, and the commercial) Tj T*
(transaction is all over. But there are other exchanges, an immense) Tj T*
(class of them, different from these in this respect, that though the) Tj T*
(transaction considered as a mere case of value created and measured is) Tj T*
(then and there ended, yet considered as to the nature of that) Tj T*
(preliminary exchange which implies and requires another future) Tj T*
(exchange to consummate it, it is not then and there ultimately closed,) Tj T*
