(buy and sell does not confine itself to what the Past offers in all) Tj T*
(its accumulated valuables, nor to what the Present unfolds in the) Tj T*
(unlimited desires and efforts of congregated men, but reaches out also) Tj T*
(into the Future, and makes that pay tribute more and more into the) Tj T*
(vast treasury of its Gains. And this too is legitimate. Man is at once) Tj T*
(and all the time actor and historian and prophet. The future is not) Tj T*
(wholly unknown. Given the one assumption, that Earth and Men go on as) Tj T*
(heretofore, Exchange knows well enough, and better and better, whom of) Tj T*
