(averages and of probabilities comes along to guide and to enhearten) Tj T*
(the investor. Any thoroughly established government of to-day can) Tj T*
(borrow all the money that it wants on its public pledge to repay the) Tj T*
(principal fifty years hence. England has borrowed millions of pounds) Tj T*
(sterling, giving no day certain in the future for its repayment. These) Tj T*
(funds are called "Consolidated Annuities": the interest on them is) Tj T*
(paid on a day nominated in the bond: the principal is to be paid when) Tj T*
(the borrower chooses, or never.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(b. The other and final peculiarity of Credit is, that it always) Tj T*
(involves on the part of one person a commercial confidence in some) Tj T*
(person _as such_. The term, Credit, is derived from the Latin CREDO,) Tj T*
(_I believe_, and the corresponding term, Debt, from DEBEO, _I owe_.) Tj T*
(Thus the personal element and the future element are wrapt up in the) Tj T*
(very origin of the words. There is no credit without debt, and no debt) Tj T*
(without credit. The very words imply a _belief_ of one of the two) Tj T*
(parties in a commercial promise made by the other, and also an) Tj T*
(_obligation_ acknowledged by this party as due to the first. There is) Tj T*
(a basis for credit in human nature. Faith in each other to a certain) Tj T*
(extent is natural to men. Whatever enlarges the intellectual) Tj T*
(foresight, and especially the moral character of men, opens a broader) Tj T*
(and surer field for Credits. Civilization, so-called, and Christianity) Tj T*
(certainly, deepens and broadens the natural trust of man in man.) Tj T*
(Despite all the instances of broken faith, and they are too many;) Tj T*
(despite the shocks and cautions that come every now and then to every) Tj T*
(man who trusts much in his fellow-men; experience itself justifies and) Tj T*
(rewards an ever-growing commercial trust. It is one of the noble) Tj T*
(things in international commerce, as we shall see, that men trust each) Tj T*
(other across the oceans, and lay millions of value upon the faith of a) Tj T*
(single firm. As the core of the Christian religion is confidence in a) Tj T*
(_Person_, so the very substance of credits is a natural and in general) Tj T*
(well-grounded faith in _persons as such_.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A Credit, then, may be defined to be _a Right to demand something of) Tj T*
(somebody_; and a Debt to be _an Obligation to pay something to) Tj T*
(somebody_. What always lies, accordingly, between creditors and) Tj T*
(debtors, are Rights coupled with Obligations; and these are) Tj T*
(_Property_, just as much as anything is and for the same reason, since) Tj T*
(they always may be, and usually are, bought and sold by other parties) Tj T*
(as well as the original parties. In these Rights or Claims,) Tj T*
(therefore, arises a commerce, domestic and foreign, immense in extent) Tj T*
(and amount, and the Rights themselves take their undisputed place on) Tj T*
(an equality with tangible Commodities and personal Services.) Tj T*
