(Valuables, by drawing two or three distinctions between Credit-Rights) Tj T*
(and some other rights very apt to be confounded with them.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(\(1\) The distinction between credit-rights and other rights is well) Tj T*
(rooted in the Latin language and in the Roman law, while the) Tj T*
(corresponding English terms are quite ambiguous and need to be used) Tj T*
(with great caution. In Latin, a true debt is called a _Mutuum_,) Tj T*
(because it lies between two persons, a creditor, and a debtor, and is) Tj T*
(a credit-right independent of the question of fact whether the debtor) Tj T*
(has now the thing rendered to him or not, indeed whether he has) Tj T*
(anything at all to pay with or not; on the other hand, a thing merely) Tj T*
(lent, when the very thing lent is to be returned to its owner, who has) Tj T*
(not in the meantime parted with his property to the other, is called) Tj T*
(in Latin a _Commodatum_. The English tongue has but the one word,) Tj T*
(_Loan_, for the two very distinct operations: for the loan of a book,) Tj T*
(for instance, which is to be returned after use, and which may be) Tj T*
(legally reclaimed by the owner if he chance to find it anywhere, that) Tj T*
(is, the Latin _commodatum_; and for the loan of money, or other such) Tj T*
(measurable thing, which is to be returned _in kind_ only, and which) Tj T*
(may _not_ legally be reclaimed except through some action of the) Tj T*
(borrower, since the ownership of that thing rendered has passed over) Tj T*
(to him completely, that is, the Latin _mutuum_. The same ambiguity of) Tj T*
(course inheres in the corresponding English word, _Borrow_. The) Tj T*
(English language is relatively poor in words expressing nice legal) Tj T*
(distinctions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Now, as a true debt is a claim on a _person_ and never on a _thing_,) Tj T*
(the Roman Law is true to the nature of things and to the vital) Tj T*
(distinctions of our science, when it names the right to which a) Tj T*
(_mutuum_ gives birth as a _jus in personam_, that is to say, a right) Tj T*
(against the person; while it names the legal obligation arising out of) Tj T*
(a _commodatum_ as a _jus in re_, that is to say, a right to the very) Tj T*
