(\(5\) A penultimate Disadvantage of Credit may be noted in the facility) Tj T*
(which it offers for contracting great national Debts. There are) Tj T*
(certain aspects, under which a Nation may be properly regarded as a) Tj T*
(moral person, and as such person may pledge the public faith for the) Tj T*
(present and the future, becoming a debtor to its own people or to) Tj T*
(foreigners, and thus a public debt may be made a sort of mortgage on) Tj T*
(the national property and income. Now, it cannot be fairly denied,) Tj T*
(that incidental advantages may spring up in connection with such a) Tj T*
(national debt: for example, the bonds, which are its evidences, may) Tj T*
(open up to the people a convenient form of investment for presently) Tj T*
(inactive capital, and for trust funds of all kinds; there can be) Tj T*
(little doubt that certain classes of persons holding these national) Tj T*
(obligations are won thereby to a stronger patriotism and become better) Tj T*
(friends to stability in government, although this consideration) Tj T*
(applies mainly to new governments and to those temporarily endangered;) Tj T*
(both England and the United States now make a portion of their public) Tj T*
(debt the basis of a national system of Banking, but it is perhaps) Tj T*
(questionable whether this can be justly put among the incidental) Tj T*
(benefits of the Debts; and again "a moderate debt adds to the credit) Tj T*
(of a Nation, and its ability to raise money in an emergency, for) Tj T*
(bankers and capitalists are more ready to take such securities as they) Tj T*
(are in the habit of dealing in" \(Sidney Homer\).) Tj T*
() Tj T*
