(lowering of the interest-rate and by the paying off of principal to) Tj T*
($61,368,912 for the fiscal year ending June 30, 1881; between March,) Tj T*
(1869, and August, 1873, the United States paid $378,015,065 on the) Tj T*
(principal of its public debt; the collection of the Internal Revenue) Tj T*
(alone of the national government cost for the fiscal year 1867,) Tj T*
($7,712,089; and in each of the two years, 1870 and 1881, a little over) Tj T*
($101,500,000 was paid out to reduce the principal of the Debt. All) Tj T*
(those vast sums came out of the industry and income of individuals;) Tj T*
(and taxation to any degree as all this implies is a mighty disturbance) Tj T*
(to industry, and gives rise to an army of officials who eat out a) Tj T*
(considerable percentage of all they collect. Moreover, the various) Tj T*
(expedients of taxation, which are always practically unequal in their) Tj T*
(operation, are apt to give rise to irritation and political agitation,) Tj T*
(and even sometimes to threats of repudiation, especially when the) Tj T*
(occasion has gone by under which the debt was contracted, and another) Tj T*
