(creating.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Here the vexed question arises, how far has one generation _the right_) Tj T*
(to throw upon succeeding ones the burdens of a National Debt? The true) Tj T*
(answer to this question is, _it has a very limited right indeed_. The) Tj T*
(opposite doctrine implies tacitly when not openly, that the succeeding) Tj T*
(generations will have no occasion for extraordinary expenses of their) Tj T*
(own, and, therefore, may rightfully be made to contribute to the) Tj T*
(extraordinary expenditures of this generation. But it is pure) Tj T*
(assumption to take for granted, that the next generations will not) Tj T*
