() Tj T*
(\(6\) The final Disadvantage of Credit is this, that it is apt to) Tj T*
(confuse the minds of men as to its own nature, from its apparent) Tj T*
(resemblance to something else, which is at bottom wholly unlike it.) Tj T*
(The people of the United States have suffered greatly from this) Tj T*
(confusion, and are likely to suffer from it still more in the time to) Tj T*
(come, both in their property and progress at home and in their good) Tj T*
(name abroad; and it becomes all good citizens, and especially all) Tj T*
(those called upon to pronounce on the Law of the Land, to know) Tj T*
(thoroughly the radical difference between a _Credit_ and a) Tj T*
(_Quittance_, and so to escape the contagious confusion that has) Tj T*
(entered and stirred up the popular, and even the judicial, mind of) Tj T*
(this country. All through the present chapter has been insisted on and) Tj T*
(illustrated the point, perhaps to the weariness of the reader, that) Tj T*
(Credit is always essentially the _Promise_ of one person to another,) Tj T*
