(Bullionism. There is not an Economist in Christendom, of any) Tj T*
(international or even national reputation, who now undertakes fairly) Tj T*
(and squarely by means of analysis and induction, to propound or defend) Tj T*
(a scheme so contrary to common sense and common honesty as this is,) Tj T*
(and which, universally applied, would annihilate the commerce of the) Tj T*
(world. But many of the nations are still tinctured more or less by the) Tj T*
(old subtlety, and powerful classes within them and specially within) Tj T*
(the United States, classes grown rich and powerful by what is nothing) Tj T*
(else than public plunder, are strenuous and successful advocates, not) Tj T*
(in open discussion and fair debate but by clandestine and corrupting) Tj T*
(methods and combinations, to maintain in the light of the nineteenth) Tj T*
(century an outworn and decrepit "something" worthy only of the dark) Tj T*
(ages. The old and foolish cry for a "balance of trade" is merged now) Tj T*
(in the United States into the insane and hateful clamor for the) Tj T*
(destruction of public trade in the behalf of private gain.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This is the sole reason why we must now undertake a careful chapter on) Tj T*
(Foreign Trade. There is no reason in the nature of things, or in the) Tj T*
(nature of trade, why Foreign Commerce should be treated of separately) Tj T*
(from Domestic Commerce. The two are precisely alike in all their) Tj T*
(principles and in all their results. In one as in the other, in every) Tj T*
(case and everywhere, there are \(1\) two persons, each of whom has a) Tj T*
(Service in his hands to sell against a Service in the hands of the) Tj T*
(other; \(2\) two reciprocal estimates, by which each owner concludes) Tj T*
(that he prefers the Service of the other to his own; \(3\) two mutual) Tj T*
(renderings, by which each Service comes into the possession, present) Tj T*
(or prospective, of the new owner; and \(4\) two personal satisfactions) Tj T*
(as the result of all, constituting the ultimate motive and the sole) Tj T*
(reward of Buying and Selling.) Tj T*
