(In the old classification of Logical Fallacies this particular one was) Tj T*
(called by the Romans "_post hoc ergo propter hoc_," that is, _after) Tj T*
(something therefore on account of that thing_. The thoughts and the) Tj T*
(speech of civilized men have always been full of some form of this) Tj T*
(incongruity of inference; but it is the stock in trade, the staple and) Tj T*
(body of protectionist argumentation. But it is utterly devoid of any) Tj T*
(significance whatever. Unless some natural tie of connection can be) Tj T*
(shown, as between precedent and consequent, unless it can be probably) Tj T*
(shown that _nothing but_ the precedent could cause the consequent,) Tj T*
(unless taxes are adapted in their very nature to increase riches,) Tj T*
(unless repeated subtractions can be shown to be the same thing as) Tj T*
(multiplied additions, then all this sickening talk of cheapening) Tj T*
(prices and intensified activities and diffused popular blessings under) Tj T*
(an odious scheme of subtle taxes that only _take_ and can never) Tj T*
(_give_, is to be treated with a silent and pitying contempt, whether) Tj T*
(used by the duped or the duping. A good instance of this empty form of) Tj T*
(reasoning,--much better because more uniform than any one ever sought) Tj T*
(to be applied in the realm of Trade,--would be this: the Day has) Tj T*
(uniformly followed after the Night ever since the dawn of Time, and) Tj T*
(therefore the Night is the cause of the Day!) Tj T*
