(legitimate beat. They have, however, justified the inclusion upon very) Tj T*
(different grounds, one from another; and so far as now appears, the) Tj T*
(present writer was the first technical Economist to disclaim in the) Tj T*
(name of his Science direct jurisdiction over Taxation.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(A careful discussion of a series of distinct though related Questions) Tj T*
(belonging to Taxes will exhibit the whole practical matter in the) Tj T*
(light of well-established principles of economical Science.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(1. What is the fundamental GROUND of Taxes? _Government_ is an) Tj T*
(essential prerequisite to any general and satisfactory Exchanges,) Tj T*
(since it contributes by direct effort to the security of person and) Tj T*
(property; and justly claims, therefore, from each citizen a) Tj T*
(compensation in return for the Services thus rendered to him. We do) Tj T*
(not mean to say that government exists solely for the protection of) Tj T*
(person and property, or that all the operations of government are to) Tj T*
(be brought down within the sphere of exchange, for government exists) Tj T*
(as well for the improvement as for the protection of society, and many) Tj T*
(of its high functions are moral, to be performed under a lofty sense) Tj T*
(of responsibility to God and to future ages; nor do we mean to say) Tj T*
(that government has not also a deep ground for its existence, in) Tj T*
(virtue of which it may on extraordinary occasions demand all the) Tj T*
(property of all, and even the lives of some, of its citizens; but we) Tj T*
(do mean to say that, whatever may be conceded as the ultimate ground) Tj T*
(of government, the matter of taxation, by which government is) Tj T*
(outwardly and ordinarily supported, and by which it takes to itself a) Tj T*
(part of the gains of every man's industry, finds a ready and solid) Tj T*
(justification in the common principles of Exchange. If, as far as the) Tj T*
(tax-payer is concerned, the exchange does not seem to be voluntary, on) Tj T*
(a closer analysis it is seen to be really voluntary; for in effect the) Tj T*
(people organize government for themselves, and voluntarily support it,) Tj T*
(and there is no government separate from the will of the people.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In a very important sense, accordingly, a tax paid is a reward for a) Tj T*
(service rendered. The service which government renders to Production) Tj T*
